  "details": "When you try to play with udon and change eye height update constantly during a period of time, locally it works as intended, but the remote players will see an avatar floating in mid-air as it changes size, and after 1.5-2 seconds the avatar will rescale for the remote player. It might be because it's the server's side that sends updates of the eye's height to the rest of clients every 1.5-2s. Is it possible to make this update in real time, or at last update more frequently?\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\nIt can be tested with this sample script put into a cube:\n\npublic class growoninteract : UdonSharpBehaviour\n\n{\n\n    float scale = 1.0f;\n\n    float finalScale = 1.0f;\n\n    float scaleFactor = 3.0f;\n\n    VRCPlayerApi playerApi;\n\n    bool grow = false;\n\n    void Start()\n\n    {\n\n        playerApi = Networking.LocalPlayer;\n\n    }\n\n    private void Update()\n\n    {\n\n        if (scale <= finalScale && grow)\n\n        {\n\n            playerApi.SetAvatarEyeHeightByMeters(scale);\n\n            scale += 0.001f;\n\n        }\n\n        else\n\n        {\n\n            grow = false;\n\n        }\n\n    }\n\n    public override void Interact()\n\n    {\n\n        scale = playerApi.GetAvatarEyeHeightAsMeters();\n\n        finalScale = scale * scaleFactor;\n\n        grow = true;\n\n    }\n\n}\n\nAffected: PC & Quest\n\nBuild number: 1312 \n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1123256890156122223/1123608993311494174/2023-06-28_15-39-32.mp4",
